            <div class="cell large-12 medium-12 small-12">
                <h2 class="text-center">UT Health San Antonio research and education </h2>
                <p class="text-center">As the sole academic health center in South Texas, we are at the forefront of joint replacement research. Our orthopaedic surgeons are active in international organizations, clinical trials and research to advance patient care. Some of our key focus areas include:</p> 
                <div class="indent-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>National registry for joint replacements</strong>: We’re active participants in the American Academy of Orthopaedic Surgeons (AAOS) <a href="https://www.aaos.org/registries/american-joint-replacement-registry/">American Joint Replacement Registry</a> (AJRR). By sharing our data on hip and knee replacements, we’re helping to improve care, safety and outcomes for patients worldwide.</li>
                        <li><strong>MISHA knee implant trial</strong>: We’re one of only a few sites participating in a nationwide clinical trial of the innovative MISHA knee system. This joint-preserving device relieves pressure on the knee to help some patients avoid total knee replacement surgery.</li>
                        <li><strong>Thumb replacement study</strong>: We’re one of four centers in the country participating in a study to track the outcomes of patients who receive thumb implants.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
           
        </div>
